"""northern_barrens: speeches for the story pass, and places named where the old accept line used to carry them."""

STORY = {
    'taurajo_centaur_wind': ("I'm Ruka, the quartermaster. I've sent three warbands north this season and had two come back.\n\nThe Kolkar are raiding the Northern Barrens road. It isn't the war camp out east, it's a different clan, and a faster one. They hit Far Watch Post, where the road bends toward Durotar, and they're gone before the garrison is off the wall. I can't spare another warband, but I can spare you.\n\nKill the Kolkar Raiders where you find them, and do it where the garrison can see. Half of holding a post is the post believing somebody's coming.", "Fight where the wall can see you. A garrison that's watched one fight fights the next one better."),
    'taurajo_outriders_warning': ("The outriders came in overnight, and I don't like what they brought.\n\nThe raiders you thinned at Far Watch were a screen. The clan itself is massing at Mor'shan Base Camp, in the north of the Northern Barrens, below the Rampart.\n\nIf they take the base camp they cut the Gold Road, and then nothing reaches Ashenvale and nothing comes back from it. The Warsong up there are fighting on what we send them.\n\nHit the raiders where they're gathering, before they've finished gathering. Their marauders on the Kolkar Plains, east of this town, are the same clan and count the same.", "Hit the stragglers on the edge of the camp first. A clan that's still gathering loses heart quickly."),
    'taurajo_windhoofs_ledger': ("I'm Grukan, and I keep the board. This one's fresh. Sergra put it up herself, and Sergra doesn't post bounties, she posts orders, so you know she's run out of people to order.\n\nIt's for the Kolkar Raiders in the Northern Barrens, a full count of them. They're the ones cutting the road to Far Watch Post in the east and massing at Mor'shan Base Camp in the north, up the Gold Road. There's no name on it, no khan or chieftain, just a number. That's the kind of bounty you post when you're not trying to win, only trying not to lose.", "Watch the long grass round Far Watch. They ride low, and you'll hear them before you see them."),
    'org_slayers_ring': ("Now for the part that isn't trade. The Witchwing Slayers out in the Dry Hills aren't ordinary harpies, and I wouldn't send you after them for feathers. They're Serena Bloodfeather's lieutenants. You'll know them by their rings, all the same make. They were given, not found.\n\nThat's a chain of command. Out here, among harpies, somebody sat down and decided who answers to whom and handed out tokens to prove it. I've hunted these hills for eighteen years and never seen harpies do that before her.\n\nSo kill the slayers first, and Serena after, not the other way round. Kill her while the slayers live, and the hills have a handful of leaders inside a month. Take the rings off them, because I want to lay them out and count.", 'Keep the rings on a cord, not loose in a pouch. I want to see which ones were worn the longest.'),
}
